# [[.Name]]

go-c8y-cli extension written in Go, using the [extension SDK](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/reubenmiller/go-c8y-cli/pkg/extsdk).

## Install

```sh
c8y extensions install <owner>/[[.Name]]
```

c8y installs the release archive for your platform. Repositories without releases are installed using git, but then the binary has to be built manually.

## Development

```sh
go build -o bin/[[.Name]] .
c8y extensions install .
c8y [[.ExtName]] services list
```

The extension is installed as a link to this folder, so rebuilding the binary is enough to see your changes.

* `extension.yaml` declares the binary and its commands
* `views/` contains views which c8y uses to display the output of the commands

Check the extension for problems, for example flags which clash with the c8y global flags:

```sh
c8y extensions validate .
```

## Release

Push a tag starting with `v` (for example `v1.0.0`). The release workflow uses [GoReleaser](https://goreleaser.com) to build an archive for each platform, with the binary and the extension files, and a `checksums.txt` file which c8y uses to verify the download.
